<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 75,181 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 75,181 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 75,181 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday, compared to 70,396 tonnes on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Saturday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			35,125	    34,175</p>
<p>    Import cargo			40,056	    36,221</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, two ships are expected to sail and ten to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Kerosin oil	   56,000	 Warbah		 due</p>
<p>Furance oil	   40,000	 Miraj		  due</p>
<p>Sulphur		 3,101	  Senyar		 due</p>
<p>Phostphate	    29,887	 Lapento Glory	due</p>
<p>Crude oil	     68,000	 Johar		  23/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
